A||||10||fierobear||Fiero crash safety and lesson learned||||1||
Z||000000||fierobear||04-07-2001||10:10 PM||||Well, I learned two things today: the Fiero is very safe in accidents<BR>*and* I probably drive too fast.<P>I was cruising on the freeway, on my way up to the Fiero Shop with<BR>George Miller (of same) in my 88GT. There was an accident up ahead, and<BR>I didn't see that people were slowing down or stopped. I hit a Toyota<BR>sedan (Camry? don't know) pretty hard from behind. I hit them so hard,<BR>that it pitched the car up onto the front of my GT. One of it's tires<BR>broke my windshield, and my hood flew over my car and landed behind me.<P>I had bought some McDonalds for breakfast and was going to eat it when I<BR>got to his shop. I placed my coffee in that spot to the right of the<BR>instrument panel. The force of the impact and the coffee leaking down<BR>made me think that some fluid was leaking in the passenger compartment.<BR>I told George "this car is finished." George looked the car over and<BR>immmediately told me no, it's not totalled and absolutely fixable. Good<BR>thing, huh?<P>OK, so the lessons learned:<P>1. Fieros are damn safe in accidents. The car in front of me ended up<BR>*on top* of my front end, and neither of us were injured, besides some<BR>sore spots. Don't let anyone tell you that a Fiero is a deathtrap. Thank<BR>God for this car. It's not even close to being totalled, and will be<BR>back on the road in no time. George and I not only walked away, we went<BR>to his shop and worked on my Formula 3.4 swap (yeah, I know, just what I<BR>need, more power and speed. Maybe I should be doing a 2.5 swap???).<P>2. I probably drive too fast and aggressive. I thought I was a good<BR>driver, haven't had any accidents until now. Well, this was my fault.<BR>Was I going too fast, not paying enough attention, following too close?<BR>I don't know. That part of the accident is kinda fuzzy, but I obviously<BR>did something wrong.<P>So, why am I sharing this story with hundreds of fellow Fiero owners?<BR>I'm the president of a Fiero club, I think I'm a good driver, and BLAM I<BR>wreck my GT in a split second. PLEASE learn from this. Humble yourself a<BR>little, don't assume you're indestructable, don't think an accident<BR>can't happen to you. It can, when you least expect it. Slow down a<BR>little, don't be so aggressive. Think, pay attention, don't think you're<BR>Mario *&^%ing Andretti. I thought I was good, safe and even hot s#&t.<BR>BLAM! Not anymore.<P>If you love your car and even your life, think about it. If anyone wants<BR>pictures of my formerly beautiful GT, I'll send them. LEARN from this,<BR>OK? I hope I will. Suddenly, I don't feel like driving so fast.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||04-07-2001||10:22 PM||||Thanks for sharing. <BR>Hope your GT's back in shape quickly.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
