Z||000003||Raydar||04-07-2001||11:03 PM||||Wow! Glad I wasn't there! <BR>J/K... Glad nobody got hurt.<BR>I'll bet that made one helluva noise. <BR>Lucky he went under, though. Made it a much "softer" hit than bumper-to-bumper. <P>But hey, that's what Camrys do best. Block the road.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000004||ElricSI||04-07-2001||11:06 PM||||I spun my Fiero on an ice patch at about 60 miles an hour.  Was on a highway with some traffic going around a curve to the RIGHT.  I was having some problems with my parking brake, and I think now one of the wheels may have locked up.  (Kinda wierd looking at another driver about 10 feet away while going backward.)  Anyway the car spun to the RIGHT, which I still don't understand.   It landed in a snow bank.  I think some of the wheel nut caps popped off, but that was it.<P>Anyone else have any Fiero crash stories?  I imagine that it is impossible to get whiplash at least, plus your legs are not mangled by the engine.<P>------------------<BR>Proud Owner of 85 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||04-08-2001||12:24 AM||||FBear, glad everyone is ok. The car can be fixed. The visible damage is all anoying BS...<P>The following IS NOT ment to be disrespectfull or start a flame war....<P>I wrecked the first car I owned. I actually bought it after I wrecked it.... Was test driving it, trashed it, liked it, bought it any way. <P>BEst thing I ever did car wise.<P>Allot of people think they are good drivers. I did when I trashed that car. (I won't go into how it was fixed. I doubt anyone would believe it anyway...) I had even been told by a number of people I was a good driver... Why should I think I wasn't....<P>Most people think they are good drivers. One hell of allot of them aren't. The biggest reason is that they are never tought how to drive in the first place. Driver training requirements used by nearly all states fall horibly short of teaching people what is actually required behind the wheel.<P>Unfortunatly even after a wreck most people still don't catch on. It's always the other peoples fault. I'm glad when I see someone that has a wreck and can admit that for whatever reason, even if they don't know how, they screwed up.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||04-08-2001||12:28 AM||||Dude, that pic is BEAUTIFUL!  Now, don't freak, I mean that by showing how safe the car is.  I'm glad you guys are ok, and the car is repairable.  It's gotta suck, but coulda been worse, huh?  Good luck getting her back on the road! ||||reg||11
