Z||000008||fyerstarter||04-08-2001||12:40 AM||||Yeah I've learned a few valuable lessons from my recklessness too. One was when I totalled my first car (69 mustang) at 16 when I had only had the car for 3 months. God I miss that car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  And then 4 years later I drove my 87 GT through a fence into a tennis court within a week of buying it :\ I still have it and you would never tell from looking at it. I think Fieros survive wrecks really well and because of the removeable body panels are pretty easy to fix.<P>As much as we all love making our cars go fast and racing the riceboys and the muscleheads don't race on the freeway or in traffic. If some punk pulls up to you at a stop light and wants to race go find somewhere else to do it where your not going to endager other peoples lives. Imagine some kids are crossing the street up ahead or an elderly lady? Almost every major metropolis has some illegal street races every Fri or Sat night along some old abandoned railroad tracks or the industrial areas...you know what I'm talkin about  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> And every rural area certainly has that quarter mile strip out by the dairys of the farmlands. <P>Then when you win you can brag about really winning the race. These stoplight street races don't means ****  anyway<P>"yeah dude we both gunned it at the light for about 50 feet and then he slowed down to let this sentra merge, and i went in the left lane and then he pulled up along side me and we were pretty even for a while but i pulled ahead when he got stuck behind a bus!"<P>THBBBBBBT   Gimme a break.||||reg||1
